{"parentUuid":"75740203-f9d0-451f-949a-58c53bc50823","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a74910df2cdb4f460","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LbqEfMwvaspkKD2FJ49i6h","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t== ARCH Engine architecture, governance & agent organization\n2\t -- ARCH.REQ Requirements & configuration profiles\n3\t    ARCH.REQ.game-requirements | Capture target game requirements (genre, scale, platforms, online model) as engine requirements | engine-architect | E | \n4\t    ARCH.REQ.profiles | Engine configuration profiles & feature sets (indie 2D → AAA open-world online) | engine-architect | E | \n5\t    ARCH.REQ.hardware-tiers | Target hardware tier definitions (portable, mobile, console, PC min/rec/high) | engine-architect | E | performance-architect\n6\t    ARCH.REQ.non-goals | Capability & non-goal register (what the engine deliberately does not do) | engine-architect | E | \n7\t -- ARCH.STRUCT Structure & boundaries\n8\t    ARCH.STRUCT.layering | Layering rules & module boundaries | engine-architect | E | \n9\t    ARCH.STRUCT.contracts | Contract registry between subsystems | engine-architect | E | \n10\t    ARCH.STRUCT.build-buy | Build / integrate / buy decisions (middleware, OSS) | engine-architect | E | architecture-governance\n11\t    ARCH.STRUCT.replaceability | Subsystem replaceability & optionality (modules absent in small profiles) | engine-architect | E | \n12\t    ARCH.STRUCT.conventions | Global conventions: units, handedness, up-axis, coordinate spaces | engine-architect | E | math-simd-numerics\n13\t    ARCH.STRUCT.arbitration | Cross-domain arbitration & escalation of boundary disputes | engine-architect | E | \n14\t -- ARCH.GOV Architecture governance\n15\t    ARCH.GOV.adr | ADR lifecycle with evidence, alternatives, revisit conditions | architecture-governance | E | \n16\t    ARCH.GOV.fitness | Automated architectural fitness functions (layering, dependency, contract conformance) | architecture-governance | E | \n17\t    ARCH.GOV.anti-legacy | Anti-legacy review of designs against flagged patterns | architecture-governance | E | \n18\t    ARCH.GOV.radar | Technology radar & maturity tiers with promotion criteria | architecture-governance | E | research-evidence\n19\t    ARCH.GOV.coding-standard | Coding standard & language subset | architecture-governance | E | core-runtime-architect\n20\t -- ARCH.EVID Research & evidence\n21\t    ARCH.EVID.grading | Source grading & provenance tiers | research-evidence | E | \n22\t    ARCH.EVID.survey | Literature survey protocol per decision | research-evidence | E | \n23\t    ARCH.EVID.spike | Prototype/spike protocol producing evidence where literature is thin | research-evidence | E | \n24\t    ARCH.EVID.claims | Benchmark-backed claims standard | research-evidence | E | perf-benchmarking\n25\t -- ARCH.ORG Agent organization\n26\t    ARCH.ORG.decomposition | Milestone → task decomposition by skill territory | program-orchestration | E | \n27\t    ARCH.ORG.ownership-ledger | Ownership ledger & territory locks | program-orchestration | E | \n28\t    ARCH.ORG.integration | Integration sequencing & milestone vertical slices | program-orchestration | E | \n29\t    ARCH.ORG.change-requests | Contract change-request protocol between agents | program-orchestration | E | architecture-governance\n30\t    ARCH.ORG.critic-gates | Scheduling critic gates per stage | program-orchestration | E | \n31\t== PLAT Platform & hardware abstraction\n32\t -- PLAT.PAL Platform abstraction layer\n33\t    PLAT.PAL.os | OS services abstraction (threads, virtual memory, files, time, dynamic libraries) | platform-architect | E | \n34\t    PLAT.PAL.cpu-topology | CPU topology & feature discovery (hybrid cores, SMT, caches, NUMA, ISA) | platform-architect | E | job-system-task-graph\n35\t    PLAT.PAL.windowing | Windowing & surfaces | platform-architect | E | \n36\t    PLAT.PAL.lifecycle | Process lifecycle (suspend, resume, constrained, terminate) | platform-architect | E | platform-console,platform-mobile-portable\n37\t    PLAT.PAL.capability-tiers | Platform capability tiers & feature query | platform-architect | E | \n38\t    PLAT.PAL.web | Web target (WASM + WebGPU) | platform-architect | M | \n39\t    PLAT.PAL.cloud-streaming | Cloud-streaming targets (latency, encode, input) | platform-architect | M | \n40\t -- PLAT.DESK Desktop & handheld PC\n41\t    PLAT.DESK.os-integration | Windows / Linux / SteamOS / macOS integration | platform-desktop | E | \n42\t    PLAT.DESK.display | Display enumeration, modes, DPI, HDR & VRR capability | platform-desktop | E | \n43\t    PLAT.DESK.handheld | Handheld PC specifics (power, resolution, controls) | platform-desktop | E | \n44\t    PLAT.DESK.server-host | Server host OS specifics (Linux containers) | platform-desktop | E | dedicated-server\n45\t -- PLAT.CON Console-class platforms\n46\t    PLAT.CON.os-memory | Console OS & memory model (UMA, reserved memory, fixed hardware) | platform-console | E | \n47\t    PLAT.CON.user-model | Console multi-user model & user/device pairing | platform-console | E | \n48\t    PLAT.CON.suspend | Suspend / resume / quick-resume | platform-console | E | \n49\t    PLAT.CON.devkit | Devkit workflows & SDK toolchains | platform-console | E | build-system-toolchains\n50\t -- PLAT.MOB Mobile & portable\n51\t    PLAT.MOB.os | iOS / Android / portable-console integration | platform-mobile-portable | E | \n52\t    PLAT.MOB.tbdr | Tile-based GPU implications (bandwidth, on-chip memory) | platform-mobile-portable | E | render-graph-scheduling\n53\t    PLAT.MOB.thermal | Thermal & power adaptivity | platform-mobile-portable | E | performance-architect\n54\t    PLAT.MOB.storage | Storage & download-size constraints | platform-mobile-portable | E | \n55\t -- PLAT.SVC Platform & online services integration\n56\t    PLAT.SVC.identity | User identity, sign-in, account linking, crossplay identity | platform-onl