{"parentUuid":"d6601415-e4c5-4e38-b82c-08b039b7ae26","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a74910df2cdb4f460","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013sLv6XRetG5rp8uLYx2Z5x","type":"tool_result","content":"===== architecture-governance\n  name : Architecture Governance\n  purpose : Runs architecture as an evidence-backed, governed process: ADR lifecycle with revisit conditions, technology radar with maturity tiers and promotion criteria, automated fitness functions (layering, dependency direction, contract conformance), anti-legacy review, coding standard.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Making the architecture decisions themselves', 'engine-architect'], ['Grading sources and running spikes', 'research-evidence'], ['Test definition of done', 'test-architect']]\n  expertise : ['ADRs', 'fitness functions', 'static dependency analysis', 'technology radar']\n===== program-orchestration\n  name : Engine Program Orchestration\n  purpose : Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Deciding architecture', 'engine-architect'], ['CI mechanics', 'ci-cd-automation'], ['Release versioning', 'build-release-architect']]\n  expertise : ['multi-agent coordination', 'work breakdown', 'integration planning', 'critical-path analysis']\n===== research-evidence\n  name : Research & Evidence\n  purpose : Research discipline for every major decision: finds and grades authoritative evidence (production talks, platform docs, peer-reviewed work, reproducible benchmarks), classifies techniques as established / emerging / experimental / speculative, and runs spikes where literature is thin.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Making the decision (the owning skill does, via an ADR)', 'architecture-governance'], ['Benchmark infrastructure', 'perf-benchmarking']]\n  expertise : ['literature review', 'SIGGRAPH/GDC/HPG corpus', 'source provenance', 'experimental design']\n===== perf-benchmarking\n  name : Benchmarking & Performance Regression\n  purpose : Benchmark harnesses (micro and representative-workload scenes), automated capture, statistical analysis (variance, significance), regression detection and bisection, dashboards.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Setting budgets', 'performance-architect'], ['CI infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\n  expertise : ['benchmark statistics', 'workload design', 'change-point detection']\n===== test-architect\n  name : Test Architect\n  purpose : Test strategy and architecture: per-subsystem test pyramid, frameworks, the test definition of done every skill must meet, contract tests, test content, coverage and mutation policy, flakiness policy.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Running pipelines', 'ci-cd-automation'], ['Performance regression', 'perf-benchmarking'], ['Rendering image validation', 'render-validation']]\n  expertise : ['test strategy', 'contract testing', 'mutation testing', 'test determinism']\n===== render-validation\n  name : Rendering Validation\n  purpose : Rendering correctness validation: golden-image tests with perceptual metrics, tolerances per GPU/driver, comparisons against the reference path tracer, graphics API validation in CI.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Fixing rendering features', 'render-architect'], ['Material furnace tests (defines them; this skill runs them)', 'material-system']]\n  expertise : ['image metrics (FLIP, SSIM)', 'GPU nondeterminism', 'reference rendering']\n===== functional-automation-soak\n  name : Functional Automation & Soak\n  purpose : Game-level automation: scripted and bot playthroughs, smoke/boot tests, soak and stability runs (memory growth, leaks), hardware/OS compatibility matrix, network harnesses and server load tests.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Unit test frameworks', 'test-architect'], ['Device-farm infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\n  expertise : ['game automation', 'bots', 'long-run stability analysis']\n===== robustness-fuzzing\n  name : Robustness & Fuzzing\n  purpose : Robustness engineering: fuzzing every untrusted-input parser (assets, packets, saves, scripts, mods), sanitizer build policy, fault injection (IO errors, OOM, device lost), concurrency stress and schedule perturbation.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Threat model', 'security-engineering'], ['Fixing parsers', 'serialization-schema']]\n  expertise : ['libFuzzer/AFL++', 'sanitizers', 'fault injection', 'TSan']\n===== certification-compliance\n  name : Certification & Compliance\n  purpose : Tracks and pre-validates external requirements: platform certification (TRC/XR/Lotcheck class), age ratings, privacy law, accessibility law (CVAA, EAA), third-party licenses and SBOM, photosensitivity testing.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Implementing platform features', 'platform-architect'], ['Implementing accessibility features', 'accessibility']]\n  expertise : ['platform requirements', 'privacy law', 'accessibility law', 'license compliance']\n===== security-engineering\n  name : Security Engineering\n  purpose : Threat modeling and trust boundaries for every untrusted input, secure-coding and memory-safety policy, supply-chain security, secrets, anti-tamper boundary, privacy engineering, mod/UGC sandbox policy.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Cheat detection', 'anti-cheat-integrity'], ['Fuzzing campaigns', 'robustness-fuzzing'], ['Transport encryption implementation', 'network-transport']]\n  expertise : ['threat modeling (STRIDE)', 'memory safety', 'SLSA/SBOM', 'privacy engineering']\n===== anti-cheat-integrity\n  name : Anti-Cheat & Game Integrity\n  purpose : Cheat resistance for online games: server-authoritative validation patterns (movement, hits, economy), rate limiting, anomaly signals, integration boundary for client anti-cheat middleware.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Replication design', 'replication'], ['Transport encryption', 'network-transport']]\n  expertise : ['cheat taxonomies', 'server validation', 'anomaly detection']\n===== observability-telemetry\n  name : Observability & Telemetry\n  purpose : Instrumentation substrate: structured logging, trace zones (CPU, GPU, IO, memory), counters and metrics, profiler integrations, in-game stats, development and live telemetry with privacy consent; zero cost when compiled out.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Crash capture', 'crash-diagnostics'], ['Debug drawing and consoles', 'visual-debugging-tools'], ['Perf budgets', 'performance-architect']]\n  expertise : ['low-overhead tracing', 'Tracy/Perfetto formats', 'telemetry pipelines']\n===== crash-diagnostics\n  name : Crash & Hang Diagnostics\n  purpose : Crash, hang and GPU-fault capture and reporting: minidumps, symbolication, bucketing and triage, GPU crash dumps, watchdogs, OOM reports, assert reporting.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Emitting GPU breadcrumbs', 'rhi-core'], ['Symbol server infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\n  expertise : ['minidumps', 'DRED/Aftermath/RGD', 'crash bucketing']\n===== determinism-replay\n  name : Determinism & Replay\n  purpose : Defines determinism levels (none, same-binary, cross-platform) per subsystem and the floating-point and parallel-execution rules that achieve them; owns input/state record-replay and desync detection.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Rollback netcode', 'prediction-rollback'], ['Deterministic math implementation', 'math-simd-numerics']]\n  expertise : ['IEEE-754 reproducibility', 'deterministic scheduling', 'state hashing']\n===== plugin-system\n  name : Plugin System\n  purpose : Plugin architecture: manifests, discovery, dependency resolution, load phases, binary vs source plugins, isolation, distribution format.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Mods & UGC', 'modding-ugc'], ['Module linking internals', 'core-runtime-architect']]\n  expertise : ['plugin architectures', 'dynamic loading', 'ABI stability']\n===== modding-ugc\n  name : Modding & UGC\n  purpose : Mod and UGC support: mod SDK, content overrides via VFS layering, sandboxed mod scripting, UGC upload and moderation boundaries, mod compatibility across patches.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Sandbox policy', 'security-engineering'], ['Script VM', 'scripting-runtime']]\n  expertise : ['mod ecosystems', 'sandboxing', 'content overrides']\n===== developer-experience-docs\n  name : Developer Experience & Documentation\n  purpose : Documentation and developer experience: API reference, architecture docs, the sample-project ladder (2D → open-world online) that doubles as integration tests, templates, onboarding, doc testing, error-message standards, DX metrics.\n  non_responsibilities : [['ADR records', 'architecture-governance'], ['Iteration-time tooling', 'hot-reload-iteration']]\n  expertise : ['technical writing', 'docs-as-code', 'sample design', 'DX metrics']\n===== ml-inference-runtime\n  name : ML Inference Runtime\n  purpose : Runtime neural-network inference shared by neural rendering, animation, audio and AI: GPU (cooperative-vector / tensor) and CPU backends, model packaging and quantization, scheduling within frame budgets, determinism characteristics.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Vendor upscalers', 'reconstruction-upscaling'], ['Neural feature design (texture, material, animation)', 'texture-streaming-vt']]\n  expertise : ['inference engines', 'quantization', 'cooperative vectors', 'ONNX']\n===== serialization-schema\n  name : Serialization & Schema Evolution\n  purpose : Binary and text formats, schema evolution and upgraders, in-place loadable layouts, canonical deterministic serialization, portability, and validation of untrusted input.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Package containers', 'package-formats-vfs'], ['Network bit packing', 'replication'], ['Save-game semantics', 'persistence-save']]\n  expertise : ['schema evolution', 'binary formats', 'parsers for untrusted input']\n===== platform-online-services\n  name : Platform & Online Services\n  purpose : Abstraction over first-party platform services and third-party online backends: identity and sign-in, achievements and presence, entitlements and store, cloud saves, matchmaking/lobby/session boundaries, remote config, moderation boundaries, media capture, crossplay identity.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Game-server hosting', 'dedicated-server'], ['Save-game content', 'persistence-save'], ['Backend implementation (outside engine scope)', 'engine-architect']]\n  expertise : ['platform SDKs', 'online service APIs', 'auth tokens']\n===== content-pipeline-architect\n  name : Content Pipeline Architect\n  purpose : Asset identity and the content pipeline: asset registry and dependency graph, deterministic incremental per-platform cooking, the cook-step contract, derived-data cache and content-addressed store, distributed cooking, content validation.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Format-specific builders (shaders, animation, clusters…)', 'shader-system'], ['Runtime loading', 'resource-streaming-architect'], ['Import formats', 'asset-import-interchange']]\n  expertise : ['build systems for data', 'content-addressed storage', 'incremental computation']\n===== physics-architect\n  name : Physics Architect\n  purpose : Physics architecture: build vs integrate decision, physics world representation and ECS integration, stepping and frame sync, determinism levels, physics LOD, materials, GPU offload evaluation; covers both 2D and 3D.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Collision algorithms', 'collision-detection'], ['Solvers', 'rigid-body-dynamics'], ['Networked physics', 'prediction-rollback']]\n  expertise : ['physics engines (Jolt, PhysX, Havok, Box2D)', 'simulation architecture']\n===== audio-architect\n  name : Audio Architect\n  purpose : Audio engine architecture and threading, device backends, voice management and virtualization, middleware decision, audio budgets.\n  non_responsibilities : [['DSP algorithms', 'audio-dsp-mixing'], ['Spatialization', 'spatial-audio-acoustics']]\n  expertise : ['real-time audio', 'lock-free audio threads', 'Wwise/FMOD']\n===== network-architect\n  name : Network Architect\n  purpose : Netcode model per game type (authoritative server, lockstep, rollback, P2P/relay), network tick and time, authority model, budgets and scale targets, protocol versioning, sharded worlds evaluation.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Transport', 'network-transport'], ['Replication mechanics', 'replication'], ['Matchmaking services', 'platform-online-services']]\n  expertise : ['netcode architectures', 'distributed systems', 'latency hiding']\n===== network-transport\n  name : Network Transport\n  purpose : UDP sockets and platform network APIs, reliability and ordering, fragmentation, congestion control, encryption and authentication, NAT traversal and relays, connection lifecycle, link simulation, QUIC/WebTransport evaluation.\n  non_responsibilities : [['What is replicated', 'replication'], ['Relay service operation', 'platform-online-services']]\n  expertise : ['UDP protocols', 'congestion control', 'DTLS/QUIC']\n===== dedicated-server\n  name : Dedicated Servers\n  purpose : Headless server builds and stripping, tick cost and multi-instance density, fleet orchestration boundary, server observability, listen servers and host migration.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Fleet operation (outside engine scope)', 'platform-online-services'], ['Server logging substrate', 'observability-telemetry']]\n  expertise : ['headless builds', 'Linux containers', 'server performance']\n===== scripting-runtime\n  name : Scripting Runtime\n  purpose : Scripting language selection, VM embedding and bindings, sandboxing, debugging and profiling, hot reload, visual scripting, AOT/JIT constraints, GC policy.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Reflection substrate', 'reflection-metadata'], ['Graph editor UI', 'graph-editor-framework']]\n  expertise : ['VM embedding (Luau, .NET, Wasm)', 'DAP', 'sandboxing']\n===== ai-behavior-perception\n  name : AI Behavior & Perception\n  purpose : Decision making (behavior trees, utility, HTN/GOAP, state trees), perception, environment queries, smart objects, AI scheduling and LOD; evaluates learned and LLM-driven agents.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Navigation', 'navigation-pathfinding'], ['ML runtime', 'ml-inference-runtime']]\n  expertise : ['game AI', 'utility theory', 'HTN planning']\n===== persistence-save\n  name : Persistence & Save Games\n  purpose : Save-game model and serialization, save versioning and migration, atomic writes, platform save APIs and quotas, cloud-save sync, persistent world-state deltas, checkpoints.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Schema evolution mechanism', 'serialization-schema'], ['Cloud service API', 'platform-online-services']]\n  expertise : ['save systems', 'crash-safe writes', 'data migration']\n===== editor-architect\n  name : Editor Architect\n  purpose : Editor architecture: process model (in- vs out-of-process runtime), editor/runtime data separation, transactions and undo/redo, selection, extension API and tool scripting, play-in-editor isolation, remote live editing, headless editor, large-project performance.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Panels and inspectors', 'editor-ui-framework'], ['World viewport tools', 'world-editor-viewport'], ['Source control', 'collaboration-version-control']]\n  expertise : ['editor architecture', 'command pattern', 'tool UX']\n===== ai-assisted-authoring\n  name : AI-Assisted Authoring\n  purpose : Evaluates and integrates AI-assisted authoring: generative asset tools, editor copilots, ML-assisted retopology/rigging/UV/LOD, provenance and licensing of generated content.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Runtime inference', 'ml-inference-runtime'], ['License compliance sign-off', 'certification-compliance']]\n  expertise : ['generative models', 'tool integration', 'content provenance']\n===== ci-cd-automation\n  name : CI/CD & Automation\n  purpose : CI pipelines, build farm and artifact storage, pre-submit and merge gating, symbol servers, device-farm orchestration, developer CLI and automation.\n  non_responsibilities : [['What tests exist', 'test-architect'], ['Perf thresholds', 'performance-architect']]\n  expertise : ['CI systems', 'build farms', 'artifact management']\n===== packaging-release-patching\n  name : Packaging, Patching & Release\n  purpose : Platform packaging and signing, store-submission artifacts, delta/chunk patching, DLC, install-on-demand, client/server/content version compatibility, CDN boundary, release rollback.\n  non_responsibilities : [['Package runtime format', 'package-formats-vfs'], ['Certification tracking', 'certification-compliance']]\n  expertise : ['platform packaging', 'binary diffing', 'content delivery']","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bdd7f038-9d28-46b9-a541-87c3fb0a37aa","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:49:04.620Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d6601415-e4c5-4e38-b82c-08b039b7ae26","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
